			How to compile RDFAmos:

1.  Download ARP2 as part of Jena2 from
http://jena.sourceforge.net/downloads.html or from
http://user.it.uu.se/~udbl/software/Jena-2.1.zip

2. Set environment variable ARP2_HOME to point to Jena 2 root directory,
   e.g. C:\Program\Jena-2.1

3. Make sure your javac compiler has version 1.4 or later!

   In your default Java is 1.3 or earlier it is possible to override
   the default setting by assigning the interface variable JAVA_HOME
   to the directory where javac.exe etc. are defined, e.g.  
     set java_home=C:\Program\Java\jdk1.5.0_01\bin\
   
4. Compile Java part of RDFAmos by running 
    compile.cmd

5. Make rdfamos.dmp by running
     mkdmp.cmd

6. Test RDFAmos by
     test.cmd

7. Run RDFAmos by
     run.cmd

